From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 20:09:57 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08069/11362] [outer-loop] file: wa30 claims 9 reproduced
 levels with no reproduction path

Found while extending the QAT-vs-Q4_K_M inducer corpus. wa30's registry entry has
reproducibility: reproduced, levels_reproduced: 9, full_game_clear: true -- and
reproduce: None, action_model: None.

Every other cleared game carries something runnable: tn36 names a 340-line
general solver script, sc25 names arc_solver_kit.reproduce with its plans and
apply fn, ka59 names its label sequence plus a checksum. wa30 has prose only.

This is the exact failure the ARC Solve Reproducibility discipline was created to
prevent -- its founding directive was "we must require capturing the winning
conditions for reproducibility ... otherwise the effort is effectively wasted",
and its gate is that only offline-reproducible levels count. Those 9 levels are
currently inside reproducible_total_levels: 183 on the strength of prose and
cannot be re-verified without redoing the RE.

Filed as record integrity, not solving: the game was almost certainly solved, the
captured artifact is what is missing. Per never-prune the claim stays and is
annotated rather than decremented; the next step is to recover the path or mark
wa30's contribution provisional.
